For each lambda term, its interpretation is Scott continuous as a map of environments.

Induct on the term. A variable is application in the function argument, and zero is constant. Successor and predecessor are ternary continuous combinations of the conditional, using continuity of the which-projection, of left injection, of successor or predecessor, and of the out-projection, together with the inductive hypothesis and a constant bottom element. A conditional is substitution of the lambda retract into a nested ternary combination of conditionals, using the four inductive hypotheses. An application is a ternary combination whose third argument substitutes the out-projection of the operator into application with the argument. An abstraction substitutes the right injection into a graph whose body is continuous by the inductive hypothesis and by continuity of the environment update, split on whether the looked-up index equals the bound numeral.
